 ],
 "notes": "Merged Amaretto (k144) into Nut liqueur with Disaronno as archetype; dissolved 'Other fruit liqueur' into Fruit liqueur; renamed 'Triple sec & curaçao' to Orange liqueur. New kind Anise liqueur (sambuca, anisette). Added Becherovka, Licor 43, Unicum, Cherry Heering and Advocaat (egg liqueur, placed under Cream liqueur) as archetypes from their Wikipedia pages. Old models became versions where they fit (Chartreuse Yellow, St Germain, Branca Menta, Wenneker Blue, Crème de cassis makers, TinShing Umeshu, Baileys Original, Tia Maria Cold Brew, Disaronno Originale, Pallini); the rest stay in m. Left out: Galliano Black/White Sambuca and Amaretto, Grand Marnier Signature Series, most Baileys seasonal flavours (kept six), Aperol Spritz (a cocktail). No Plymouth Sloe Gin versions (Wikipedia confirms only that one exists). Wenneker, Senior & Co, Pierre Ferrand, Gabriel Boudier and other version makers have no register entry (no retrieved page). Sloe gin cousins patxaran and Schlehenfeuer not added (patxaran belongs with anise spirits/fruit liqueurs if wanted)."
